Z||000010||1FST2M6||02-27-2000||01:37 AM||||We have been toying with the idea of a twin set-up on my car. we have the spare turbos at the shop but not sure about engine managment. The guys at PMS are personal friends of the guys at the tuning shop i use. The PMS facility is about 15 minutes from my house in Acworth Ga. I have Nitrous and its nice and all but it runs out... turbos don't. The Shop i go to is the worlds only builder of a Twin-Turbo Civic so i'm not really worried about lack of fabricating experiance (sp) We are also shooting foa decent streetable car with the lesser T-25 or a pair of Super 16G. That 510 is nice but not what i had in mind.. thats a bit too much... if at all i'll start small and learn how to drive it before making it REALLY STUPID FAST! Also have acces to air-water intercoolers but it would be linked to the engine cooling system not a seperate glycol system... sweet idea though! What made you choose a single T-03? It has an internal waste gate right?  vacuum regulated to what boost? and what compression ratio are you running... well i'll hold on the rest of the questions till later... thanks for all the info.. Have you had your car run up on a Dyno? If so what are your numbers? ||||reg||1
