Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||02-27-2000||02:36 AM||||geez.. that IS an ugly car.<P>engine sure sounds awesome tho!!<P>and the stuff about the carbon fiber panels was very interesting to read. I might try that sometime.. depends how expensive carbon fiber is.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I've worked with bondo before, but not fiberglass.||||reg||1
Z||000013||fierosound||02-27-2000||03:41 AM||||Those Datsuns were quite boxy for sure.  BUT they were among the first affordable cars with a full independant suspension.  That's why they were very popular as rally cars.||||reg||10
Z||000014||turbo86se||02-27-2000||10:48 AM||||I've got a Miller Woods turbo on my 86SE. It's been on the car for many years and is very reliable and always there for some serious speed when I need it. The only problem I've had is the automatic transmission. I'm on my second one, and it doesn't shift as firm as my 88 coupe, I'm also nervous about a "static" noise it makes in drive sometimes. It'll come out, eventually and be rebuilt with a shift-kit. Maybe I'll wait until I put the 3.4 block in there with the turbo  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Naaa, it's almost too much for me now! As with the intercooler, I've had a few talks with IRM president Jim Sutter (owns the company that installed and sold me my turbo), and he said I really shouldn't need an intercooler, my system is set-up to run without one. So far I've ported and polished the manifolds, coated them by Jet Hot, removed the cat. convertor, ultimate motor mount, and a good tune up. At 51,110.8 miles, she's a screamer!  Check it out at   <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=226077&a=1676370" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=226077&a=1676370</A> <BR>I'll have more pics soon, of my and many Fieros. If anyone is going to the Fiero show (hosted by FOSEVA) in Williamsburg,VA in June, you'll see me there! ||||reg||10
Z||000015||Raydar||02-27-2000||02:52 PM||||Shiner... I've seen that car. The previous owner had a business that required the use of a two-way radio. We (my previous job) installed the radio equipment. The car was truly amazing. The chevy V-6 looked "factory". Well, as "factory" as a twin-turbo 2.8 can look in a 510.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||1FST2M6||02-27-2000||06:12 PM||||Turbo86SE... what are you using for Fuel managment and ignition mapping? I wcan assume that you running a MAP sensor out of a GN or sunbird turbo? What is the max PSI your wastegates are set too? Have you thought of a piggy back HKS EVC-IV or a Greddy Profect-B (piggy back electronic/vacuum wastegate controllers)Or a simple MSD BTM? Have you run you car on a Dyno? Ever come to the Atlanta area? Did you have to upgrade your cooling system to handle the increased heat created by the combustion temps?  Sorry for the 20 questions...  Thanks in advance<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||turbo86se||02-28-2000||11:39 AM||||1FST2M6, as far as I know I'm using the stock MAP sensor, I've never had to replace it. I haven't had to do any additional cooling modifications, the center bearing housing is cooled by the engine coolant. I've never had the car on a dyno, that would be interesting. I've only been into Atlanta once, spent a weekend there in Duluth. Never driven a Fiero there, yet. I'm running around 10 psi at full boost, and fuel management is stock.  If you ever take a trip to Myrtle Beach, LMK, we'll have to get together!||||reg||1
Z||000018||1FST2M6||02-28-2000||01:57 PM||||10psi! thats a lot of air! No detination issues or nothing.. thats pretty sweet.. I'll get in touch with you probly later this spring i need a vacation... If you are back in the duluth area tell me and another 20 minuts of driving and i'll see about strapping her down on the dyno... Who did you get your kit form? And do they have a web page?  if you want more info on where we'd run your car... <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>   the shop has built MANY crazy turbo cars and I'd really like mine on that list... ||||reg||1
